The '''Navassa Arsenal''' ({{lang-bl|Arsenal de Navassa}}; {{lang-ec|Arsenál de Navaza}}), is one of five operating [[W:Shipyard|shipyards]] of the [[Confederal Navy]]. It is the navy's headquarters in [[Estuaria]], and is located northeast of the city of [[Navassa]]. Founded on 14 March 1683, the Arsenal is the oldest continuously operating naval shipyard in the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. Today, most of its work concerns the overhaul, repair, and modernization of [[W:Submarines|submarines]].

In addition to its support of submarines, the Arsenal provides berthing and shore side support to surface ships, as well as maintenance and training for units of the [[Confederal Aerospace Force|Aerospace Force]]. Since 2015, it has been home to the largest training facility in Balisca for [[W:military diving|military diving]]. 

